From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MyNaai Dev <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Admin panel: category manager + bulk product upload

Two additions to Shop Products, both admin-only. Nothing here changes what a
customer sees, except that the catalogue can finally be filled at a sensible
pace — and that the shop's filter is now the panel's list.

1 · Categories (`Shop Products → Categories`)

A small manager over `shop_categories` — the ONE list the website and the app
read. Adding a category here makes it appear in the customer's shop filter on
the next load, with this label and this position, and with no deploy.

  · Order is `sortOrder`; the arrows write it. There is no second "display
    order" to keep in step with.
  · Renaming changes the LABEL only. The dialog says so next to the field
    ("stays `hair-care` if you rename it"), because the id is a slug fixed at
    creation and every product stores it.
  · The eye hides a category (`isActive: false`): it leaves the shop filter but
    stays on the products already filed under it, and stays visible here.
  · Deleting is refused while products use it — the API answers with the count,
    and the dialog then asks "move them to…" and retries with `reassignTo`. A
    category deleted out from under a product is exactly the "wrong shelf"
    complaint this whole feature exists to fix.
  · Free-text values no category owns are listed as `unmatched` with a count:
    the to-do list for finishing the tidy-up.

The product editor's Category select now reads the same list, so a new category
is selectable immediately and a product filed here is findable on the website. A
product still holding an old free-text shelf shows that value as
"(not in the list)" instead of silently blanking.

`src/utils/productCategory.js` — the hard-coded array of eight long labels that
used to feed that select — is deleted. With two lists there are two answers, and
that is how "herbal hair oil filed under HAIR COLOUR" happened.

2 · Bulk add (`Shop Products → Bulk add`)

Download the sample → fill it in → drop it back → read a per-row report → import
→ undo if it was a mistake.

  · "Check file" runs the import with `dryRun: true`: it writes nothing and
    answers the report. The button that writes names the exact number
    ("Import 112 products"), so an import is impossible without a dry run first.
  · The report shows the SHEET'S row number (the one the admin can find in
    Excel), the column and a fixable message, and offers itself as a CSV to fix
    and re-upload.
  · The choice for names that already exist (skip / update) is remembered from
    the last import.
  · A big import does not block the panel: the dialog stays dismissable, and a
    toast reports the outcome when it finishes. The product list refreshes, and
    the dialog offers "Undo this import" for the `importId` the API returned.
  · The image spec is printed inline (square 1200×1200 JPG, white background,
    ≤250 KB, up to four photos, the first is the cover) — most bad rows are
    photos, not data.

Files

  new  src/components/ShopCategoriesModal.jsx   the manager
  new  src/components/ShopBulkImportModal.jsx   sample → drop → report → import → undo
  mod  src/pages/ShopProducts.jsx               the two buttons, the category label
                                                column, refresh after an import
  mod  src/components/ShopProductModal.jsx      the category select reads the server
  mod  src/services/communication.jsx           shopCategoryAPI; shopProductAPI
                                                gains bulkTemplate / bulkImport /
                                                bulkUndo
  del  src/utils/productCategory.js             the old hard-coded list

Backend it talks to: /api/shop-categories/admin/* and
/api/shop-products/bulk/{template,import,undo} (patches
`backend-1-shop-categories.patch` and `backend-3-shop-bulk-products.patch`).

Verified: `vite build` passes with both dialogs in the bundle.
